Core Components

1. CLI

The CLI is the primary entry point for developers.

Responsibilities:

Initialize Ohira

Trigger analysis

Generate reports

Manage plugins

Display diagnostics


Example:

ohira init
ohira analyze
ohira report
ohira doctor
ohira context


---

2. REST API

Provides programmatic access to Ohira's knowledge.

Endpoints:

GET  /health
GET  /status
GET  /context
GET  /report
GET  /plugins
POST /analyze

Future versions may expose GraphQL alongside REST.


---

3. Core Engine

The orchestration layer responsible for coordinating every subsystem.

Responsibilities:

Load configuration

Discover plugins

Execute analysis pipeline

Handle errors

Manage caching

Persist knowledge


The Core Engine should remain lightweight and stable.


---

4. Project Scanner

Discovers the project environment.

Detects:

Root directory

Package manager

Language

Framework

Repository

Configuration files


Example detection:

package.json
next.config.ts
tsconfig.json
prisma/schema.prisma
docker-compose.yml
.git


---

5. Plugin Loader

Discovers and loads installed plugins.

Responsibilities:

Validate compatibility

Resolve dependencies

Register analyzers

Handle plugin lifecycle

Isolate plugin failures


Plugin lifecycle:

Discover
↓

Validate
↓

Load
↓

Initialize
↓

Analyze
↓

Unload


---

6. Analyzer Pipeline

The heart of Ohira.

Pipeline:

Project

↓

Scanner

↓

Plugins

↓

Collectors

↓

Normalizers

↓

