---

Error Handling Strategy

Ohira should never fail because one plugin fails.

Instead:

Log the error

Disable the failing plugin for the session

Continue analysis

Report the issue to the user



---

Caching Strategy

To improve performance:

Cache dependency analysis

Cache Git metadata

Cache framework detection

Perform incremental analysis when possible



---

Security Considerations

Local-first by default.

Explicit opt-in for cloud synchronization.

Sensitive values in .env files are masked.

Plugins operate under a permission model in future versions.



---

Scalability

The architecture is designed to scale from:

Small personal repositories

Medium startup projects

Large enterprise monorepos


Future distributed analysis workers can be added without redesigning the core.


---

Architecture Goals

The system should be:

Modular

Extensible

Testable

Performant

Secure

AI-ready

Framework-agnostic



---

Architecture Motto

> "One Core. Many Plugins. Infinite Projects."



This principle ensures that Ohira remains lightweight while supporting an ever-growing ecosystem of languages, frameworks, and tools.
